WEBVTT

00:01:59.248 --> 00:02:01.661
and now you can drive
to Jupiter and back twice.

00:02:01.685 --> 00:02:05.976
(Laughter)

00:02:06.449 --> 00:02:07.976
World population,

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.017
PC placements,

00:02:10.711 --> 00:02:12.975
the archive of all of medical literature,

00:02:13.497 --> 00:02:14.697
Moore's law,

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:17.048
the old way of sequencing,

00:02:17.072 --> 00:02:18.829
and here's all the new stuff.

00:02:18.853 --> 00:02:20.194
Guys, this is a long scale;

00:02:20.218 --> 00:02:22.976
you don't typically see
lines that go up like that.

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:26.900
So the worldwide capacity
to sequence human genomes

00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:30.093
is something like 50,000 to 100,000
human genomes this year.